26","16:27","16:28","16:29","16:30","16:31"],"en":{"16:19":"Now there was a rich man dressed in purple and fine linen, who lived each day in joyous splendor.","16:20":"And a beggar named Lazarus lay at his gate, covered with sores","16:21":"and longing to be fed with the crumbs that fell from the rich man’s table. Even the dogs came and licked his sores.","16:22":"One day the beggar died and was carried by the angels to Abraham’s side. And the rich man also died and was buried.","16:23":"In Hades, where he was in torment, he looked up and saw Abraham from afar, with Lazarus by his side.","16:24":"So he cried out, ‘Father Abraham, have mercy on me and send Lazarus to dip the tip of his finger in water and cool my tongue. For I am in agony in this fire.’","16:25":"But Abraham answered, ‘Child, remember that during your lifetime you received your good things, while Lazarus received bad things. But now he is comforted here, while you are in agony.","16:26":"And besides all this, a great chasm has been fixed between us and you, so that even those who wish cannot cross from here to you, nor can anyone cross from there to us.’","16:27":"‘Then I beg you, father,’ he said, ‘send Lazarus to my father’s house,","16:28":"for I have five brothers. Let him warn them, so that they will not also end up in this place of torment.’","16:29":"But Abraham replied, ‘They have Moses and the Prophets; let your brothers listen to them.’","16:30":"‘No, father Abraham,’ he said, ‘but if someone is sent to them from the dead, they will repent.’","16:31":"Then Abraham said to him, ‘If they do not listen to Moses and the Prophets, they will not be persuaded even if someone rises from the dead.’”"}}},"pairs":{},"minor":[]}